<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa Cargo May load factor down 0.2pt.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa Cargo May load factor down 0.2pt.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lufthansa Cargo saw a 0.2 percentage point fall in its freight load factor to 64.6 percent in May, parent company Deutsche Lufthansa AG said.</p>
<p>Total freight tonnage slumped 3.3 percent to 132,000 tonnes last month but capacity was also reduced, the monthly Lufthansa traffic report said.</p>
<p>&quot;Business at Lufthansa Cargo improved due to a significant improvement in average yields on the previous year's level,&quot; it noted.</p>
<p>The following tables show Lufthansa Cargo 1997 traffic figures.</p>
<p>May</p>
<p>    Cargo/mail (1,000t)	    132.5     down 3.3 pct</p>
<p>    Available tonne-km (million) 790	 down 2.9 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue tonne-km (million)   510	 down 3.1 pct</p>
<p>    Cargo load factor (pct)	64.6	down 0.2 pct pts</p>
<p>    Europe (1,000t)		  58.4	down 6.1 pct</p>
<p>    Americas (1,000t)		36.8	up 1.8 pct</p>
<p>    Asia/Pacific (1,000t)	  33.9	up 0.1 pct</p>
<p>Jan-May</p>
<p>    Cargo/mail (1,000t)	    674.8     down 0.1 pct</p>
<p>    Available tonne-km (million) 3,809     up 1.7 pct</p>
<p>    Revenue tonne-km (million)   2,562     up 0.5 pct</p>
<p>    Cargo load factor (pct)	67.3	down 0.8 pct pts</p>
<p>    Europe (1,000t)		  303.0     down 2.9 pct</p>
<p>    Americas (1,000t)		181.1     up 3.9 pct</p>
<p>    Asia/Pacific (1,000t)	  167.1     up 0.9 pct</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017 - www.racs.com</p>
